{"id": "EUVD-2026-96575", "enisaUuid": "e1562b51-e9df-3b0f-8a9a-72bac6f82440", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the SysDepartController appImportExcel handler that allows any authenticated user to import departments. Low-privileged attackers can upload a crafted Excel workbook to POST /sys/sysDepart/appImportExcel to create arbitrary sys_depart records in the administrator-maintained department tree.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:01:31", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_c091_sysdepart_appimport_xlsx.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/SysDepartController.java#L682-L717", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-sysdepart-appimportexcel"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108636", "GHSA-ww57-4vw8-q38h"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e5389438-7fca-30e9-8b23-f11c0b7516ee", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4e5c7dcb-0ffe-31a2-899f-0a4f7949631b", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}